75:[[],["$","$L41",null,{"className":"case-jobs__arrival","children":["$","$L86",null,{"headingLevel":3,"intro":["The product has three jobs. Each has its own place in the main navigation: Time, Reports and Accounting."],"jobs":[{"line":"Hours logged against a project and a client","media":{"id":"productively-pillar-track","type":"image","src":"/productively/wall/time-tracker-active-project-based.webp","alt":"Productively time tracker, project-based: a timer at two hours fifteen minutes with project, client, task and subtask chips and a billable switch, a users filter open, and a table of logged entries with duration, billable and status.","provenance":"production","width":1080,"height":768,"aspectRatio":"1080 / 768","caption":"Time Tracker tab: a running timer, the users filter open, and the logged entries below."},"text":"The timer runs against a project, a client, a task and a subtask, and one switch marks the hours billable. Below it, each logged entry shows its duration, whether it is billable and its status, Logged or Submitted. Above the entries sit a date range and a search, with filters for clients, projects, users and tags.","title":"Track time"},{"line":"The same hours as totals, a daily chart and groups","media":{"id":"productively-pillar-report","type":"image","src":"/productively/wall/reports-analysis.webp","alt":"Productively reports analysis: total, billable and non-billable hours for a period, with a daily chart and grouping by client, project and task.","provenance":"production","width":1080,"height":768,"aspectRatio":"1080 / 768","caption":"Reports analysis: three totals, a bar for each day, and the grouping table."},"text":"Analysis takes a date range, filtered by client, project and user, and shows total, billable and non-billable hours, a bar for each day, and the hours grouped by client, project, task and subtask. Two dashboards follow: Business, with cost, profit and invoiced revenue, and Team, with each member's hours against capacity.","title":"Report and visualize"},{"line":"Logged hours priced into an invoice","media":{"id":"productively-pillar-invoice","type":"image","src":"/productively/wall/receivables-add-invoice-step-1.webp","alt":"Productively Add Invoice dialog, step 1: bill number, dates and service description; a table of projects with approved and unapproved, billable and non-billable hours and total expense; options for all or approved hours, all or billable hours, how to show hours and expenses, and attaching the timelog and expense reports.","provenance":"production","width":1080,"height":768,"aspectRatio":"1080 / 768","caption":"Add Invoice, step 1: each project's hours by approval and billable, and the choice of which hours to bill."},"text":"Step one of an invoice lists each project's hours, approved and unapproved, billable and non-billable, beside its expenses. Step two gives each project one line, its duration times its charge rate, then adds tax and a discount. Receivables show the paid and overdue totals, and each invoice is marked Created, Sent, Paid or Overdue.","title":"Invoice and get paid"}],"label":"Three jobs of the product"}]}],[]]
